Id: cont009i
Severity: INFO
Category: containers
Check: check_containers
References: https://docs.docker.com/engine/security/rootless/

The Docker daemon runs as root, as it does by default. A process that
escapes a container then lands as root on the host, and every member of
the docker group is root in effect (cont001w). Rootless mode runs the
daemon and its containers as an ordinary user, so an escape lands as
that user; Podman runs rootless by default for ordinary users. Rootless
mode has limits (ports below 1024, some network modes, some storage
drivers), which is why this is informational.
